{"content":[{"c":["BASEMATH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Daughter of Elon the Hittite. Basemath was a Canaanite woman whom Esau married against his parents’ wishes (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.26.34","r":"Gen.26.34","rawR":"Gen.26.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.26.34","value":"Gen.26.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 26:34"},"). Basemath may be the same as Elon’s daughter Adah, or perhaps was her sister (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.2","r":"Gen.36.2","rawR":"Gen.36.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.2","value":"Gen.36.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Ishmael’s daughter, who married Esau (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.3","r":"Gen.36.3","rawR":"Gen.36.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.3","value":"Gen.36.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:3"},") and bore Reuel to him (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.4,10","r":"Gen.36.4,10","rawR":"Gen.36.4,10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.4,10","value":"Gen.36.4,10"}],"t":"ref","v":"4, 10"},"). This Basemath is probably the same as Ishmael’s daughter Mahalath (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.28.9","r":"Gen.28.9","rawR":"Gen.28.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.28.9","value":"Gen.28.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:9"},"). Since Ishmael was the son of the patriarch Abraham, this marriage would have been more acceptable to Isaac and Rebekah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.6-8","r":"Gen.36.6-8","rawR":"Gen.36.6-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.6-8","value":"Gen.36.6-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:6-8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MahalathPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MahalathPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MahalathPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Mahalath (Person) #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["Identifications of #1 and #2 above are somewhat confused. Most scholars suspect that Esau married Elon’s daughter Adah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.2-4","r":"Gen.36.2-4","rawR":"Gen.36.2-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.2-4","value":"Gen.36.2-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:2-4"},"), who was also called Basemath (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.26.34","r":"Gen.26.34","rawR":"Gen.26.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.26.34","value":"Gen.26.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:34"},"). Later, Esau married Ishmael’s daughter Mahalath (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.28.9","r":"Gen.28.9","rawR":"Gen.28.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.28.9","value":"Gen.28.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:9"},"), who was likewise called Basemath (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.3-4","r":"Gen.36.3-4","rawR":"Gen.36.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.3-4","value":"Gen.36.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:3-4"},"). That two of Esau’s wives should be named Basemath could be because Esau chose to give both the same affectionate name, which means “fragrant.”"],"sourceClass":"sp","t":"p"},{"c":["3. King Solomon’s daughter who married Ahimaaz, the king’s administrator in Naphtali (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.15","r":"1Kgs.4.15","rawR":"1Kgs.4.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.15","value":"1Kgs.4.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-space","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Basemath","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 26:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.26.34","rawQueryValue":"Gen.26.34","sourceRefExact":"Gen.26.34"},{"anchorText":"36:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.2","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.2","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.2"},{"anchorText":"Gn 36:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.3","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.3","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.3"},{"anchorText":"4, 10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.4,10","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.4,10","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.4,10"},{"anchorText":"28:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.28.9","rawQueryValue":"Gen.28.9","sourceRefExact":"Gen.28.9"},{"anchorText":"36:6-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.6-8","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.6-8","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.6-8"},{"anchorText":"Gn 36:2-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.2-4","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.2-4","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.2-4"},{"anchorText":"26:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.26.34","rawQueryValue":"Gen.26.34","sourceRefExact":"Gen.26.34"},{"anchorText":"28:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.28.9","rawQueryValue":"Gen.28.9","sourceRefExact":"Gen.28.9"},{"anchorText":"36:3-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.3-4","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.3-4","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.3-4"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.15","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.15","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"efeb23a2a683478244b8a536d2aaf0841d6320c5a2ac9815703ac409e765cef6","sourceItemName":"Basemath","sourceItemOrder":96,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Basemath","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Basemath","title":"Basemath","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}